/target
**/*.rs.bk
.env
node_modules/
web/dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
# Runtime artefacts (uploaded originals + the Tantivy index). **No leading slash**: `/data`
# only matches the repo root, while the server creates data/ in whatever directory it was
# started in -- that is exactly how `web/data` leaked in (30 files, two of them uploaded test
# documents). Same class of mistake as `_bench_*` missing `_holmes2.json`
data/
# docs/ is the local scratch area; only the decision records and the pipeline reference go in.
# It has to be written as /docs/* and not /docs -- once a parent directory is ignored, a
# sub-path cannot be brought back in with !.
/docs/*
!/docs/decisions/
!/docs/pipeline.md
.claude/

# Output of the measurement bench and of throwaway scripts. **Ignored wholesale by prefix**:
# previously only _bench_* was listed, and _holmes2.json made it into one commit
_*.json
_*.err
_*.sse
_*.tmp
_*.out
_*.sh
_*.txt

# wiki-history is the corpus used for benchmark runs; neither the text nor the manifest goes
# into the repo: the text is about 7MB of CC BY-SA prose, and the manifest is the product of
# one sampling run. To reproduce it, run fetch-wiki-history.mjs -- `--manifest` writes the
# manifest, `--from-manifest` rebuilds it byte for byte from the manifest (action=parse&oldid
# is immutable).
/scripts/bench/corpora/wiki-history.json
/scripts/bench/corpora/wiki-history.manifest.json
# The subsets carved out by subset-corpus.mjs are the same: the product of a manifest plus one
# line of command, not source material. The command goes into the benchmark record; the corpus
# itself does not go into the repo.
/scripts/bench/corpora/wiki-*-subset.json
/scripts/bench/corpora/wiki-nov2023.json
